                                                                          Following the elimination of the herbicide, the weeds commence growth, thereby engaging
                                                                      in a competitive relationship with the wheat. Due to the weeds’ frequently inedible nature, the
                                                                      bioenergy yield of wheat experiences a decline, resulting in a diminution of the energy source for
                                                                      the food web. This, in turn, impacts the subsequent stability of the entire ecosystem. To that end,
                                                                      the competitive relationship between wheat and weeds was simulated using the Lotka-Volterra




