7     Organic Agriculture Impacts Evaluation (OAIE) Model
                                  号



    The adoption of environmentally sustainable practices is an inevitable consequence of the pur-
suit of sustainable development. In this section, a comprehensive fuzzy integrated evaluation sys-
tem of the impacts of organic agriculture is established. This system is based on real data collected
                    信




on organic and conventional agriculture, selecting multi-level indicators. Building upon the find-
ings of prior studies, this analysis will assess the broader ecosystem impacts of organic agriculture.
                   微




7.1    Indicator Identification and Data Collection
    A comprehensive data set was meticulously assembled, encompassing conventional agriculture
prior to 2010 and organic agriculture following 2020. This endeavor involved a synthesis of in-
formation from the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO) database
and relevant specialized literature. The data were categorized into four major aspects: ecosystem,
crop growth, environmental protection, and cost-effectiveness. And ten secondary indicators were
selected below in Figure 13.
